            <aside class="key">
                <h3>Placement key</h3>
                <dl class="key-list">
                    <div class="key-item">
                        <dt>Measured bay and fixture</dt>
                        <dd>
                            Keep the 26-inch wing span centered in the 36-inch bay and the fixture’s
                            long axis aligned window-to-room. The dashed box is the advertised 24 ×
                            48-inch working footprint, not a measured PPFD boundary.
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="key-item">
                        <dt>Three surfaces run end to end</dt>
                        <dd>
                            Put the round table at the window end and both wooden tables toward the
                            room, then align their centerlines under the fixture’s long axis. They
                            are not side by side across the 36-inch bay. Their 24-inch diameter plus
                            two 16-inch table depths nominally uses about 56 inches of the
                            approximately 60-inch length. The remainder disappears quickly into real
                            gaps and leg interference.
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="key-item">
                        <dt>Paired fans stay on divider poles</dt>
                        <dd>
                            Keep both rigid mounts clear of the Mylar, offset their heights and
                            arcs, and aim from opposing directions. Exact hub heights remain
                            measurements to log.
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="key-item">
                        <dt>Camera stays on the right wall</dt>
                        <dd>
                            Frame all three surfaces lengthwise from the wall. Keep the window out
                            of the center of the time-lapse.
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="key-item">
                        <dt>Mylar is installed</dt>
                        <dd>
                            The left panel runs top-to-bottom. The floor sheet is only a carpet
                            liner; keep trays above it and its aisle edge flat.
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="key-item">
                        <dt>Air treatment stays room-side</dt>
                        <dd>
                            Start the Core Mini-P on the divider side and the DH-CS01 on the
                            white-wall side, beyond the second wooden table and nominal bay. Use
                            separate rigid trays, keep the intakes open, and move both farther into
                            the room if the real fit narrows the aisle.
                        </dd>
                    </div>
                </dl>
            </aside>
